00:02:21.760 --> 00:02:28.480
On November 3rd, Florida House District 46 votes again on the same three names from 2024.

00:02:29.180 --> 00:02:34.300
Democrat Jose Alvarez, Republican Michael Cruz, and nonpartisan Ivan Rivera.

00:02:35.020 --> 00:02:40.260
The district covers Northwest Oceola County, including Kissimmee, Poinsiana, and St.

00:02:40.460 --> 00:02:42.720
Cloud, plus a small piece of Orange County.

00:02:43.260 --> 00:02:49.720
Alvarez won last time with 57%, Cruz took 39.6 and Rivera 3.4.

00:02:49.720 --> 00:02:55.760
On August 18, he took 66% of the Democratic primary against Robert Lawane Johnson.

00:02:56.420 --> 00:03:04.640
State records cited by the Orlando Sentinel put Democrats at 42% of registered voters there and Republicans at about 21%.

00:03:04.640 --> 00:03:11.280
Alvarez, a former Cassimi mayor and a Biden-era housing department regional administrator for the Southeast and Caribbean,

00:03:11.740 --> 00:03:15.820
says a second term would stay on affordable housing, healthcare, and public safety.

00:03:15.820 --> 00:03:21.160
He points to a veteran's housing bill, money for vertiports, and a recall process for

00:03:21.160 --> 00:03:22.500
community development boards.

00:03:22.880 --> 00:03:29.040
He opposes Amendment 3, which needs 60% of voters to add a $150,000 homestead exemption

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:36.160
in 2027, rising to $250,000 in 2028, and to limit local spending to core services.

00:03:36.720 --> 00:03:41.080
He says the legislative backers could not explain how local governments would replace the lost

00:03:41.080 --> 00:03:45.160
